WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Surgery and activation are different steps.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:08.140
During surgery, the array is placed and telemetry checks device function.

00:00:08.715 --> 00:00:13.115
The lecture slide places activation two to four weeks later.

00:00:13.755 --> 00:00:16.635
At activation, sound can seem strange.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.260
Understanding speech immediately is not guaranteed.

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:28.045
Mapping adjusts electrical stimulation, with threshold levels and upper comfortable levels helping define the usable range.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.300
Follow-up combines programming with measurements of hearing and speech performance.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:40.580
Remember three separate time variables: age when hearing loss began, age at implantation, and duration of implant use.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.310
They describe different parts of the person's experience.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.520
Also separate the device arrangements.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.900
Binaural means hearing with two ears.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.865
Bimodal means a cochlear implant on one side and a hearing aid on the other.

00:00:56.305 --> 00:01:00.625
Bilateral cochlear implants means one implant in each ear.

